  "details": "In terms of Simplicity Standard Lite, works great for those who utilizes all them slots it provides.\n\nBut what about those whos are more so specific and don't need all of them?\n\nCourse there is ToonLit ....Brightens the Texture unless the Texture it's self is modified and given fake shadows in areas, otherwise it don't generate or simulate shadows.....\n\nMapcap Lit, just 1 more feature than Diffused ... though in description mainly for Metal...can be used on skins as well.. to give simulated shadows...\n\nBut both of them are missing something.....The ability to Hue shift....\n\nThe Standard Lite can do the Hue Shift with Emissive Colors or Abedo colors\n\n       but when it comes to shadows, It doesn't give you the option to sharpen the shadow's edge to give it more so a toon like or Cel Shading effect.\n\nAs title propose\n\nA Standard Lite with Matcaps\n\nOr\n\nMatcap Lit with Emissive Color.",
